+"""Unchanged methods text used by current representative-image selection."""
+METHODS = "## Representative images added on 2026-09-22\n\nThe three saved state labels are State 0, State 1 and State 2. They are not\nrenumbered as State 1/2/3. Images are illustrations of existing assignments,\nnot independent validation or mechanistic labels.\n\nThe population remains the 1,626 primary-group cells from 20 wells. The original\n97-feature state-model matrix and all saved assignments are unchanged. Images\nwere traced only to cells retained after the previously verified duplicate-row\nremoval. The heatmap artwork is retained exactly from the existing Panel E.\n\n### Reproducible selection\n\nAll primary cells are ranked within their existing state by\n`sqrt(mean_j((z_cell,j - m_state,j)^2))` across all 97 original standardized\nfeatures. `m_state,j` is the saved primary profile: within-well/state medians,\nthen median across represented wells. There is no new scaling, clustering or\ninferential test. This ranking uses the complete feature profile, not a chosen\nmechanistic feature. Cell ID breaks exact ties.\n\nThe user's requested source preference is explicit: State 0 and State 2 from\nP3-Control/P3-H1N1, and State 1 from P9-Control/P9-H1N1. These passage choices\nconstrain illustration selection; they do not establish passage specificity.\nCells flagged by the existing edge-touching or saturation QC are not eligible\nas images. Extreme-feature flags remain visible and do not automatically\nexclude a state. The complete ranking retains every primary record and all\neligibility flags; no cell is deleted from any scientific analysis.\n\nThe first four eligible candidates per state were reviewed in rank order. The\nfirst with a visually distinguishable target nucleus and visible surrounding\nsignal under the shared display settings was chosen. State 1's first candidate\nwas passed over because surrounding FITC signal was too faint for a clear\nmultichannel illustration. State 2's first candidate had closely adjacent\nnuclei and overlapping surrounding signal. All 12 candidates and decisions\nare retained in Figure S7J-L and Table S8, including the unused candidates.\nThis involves documented visual judgment and is not a fully automatic or\nblinded selection, nor a claim to have found a unique best representative.\n\n| Saved label | Existing group | Well / object | Eligible preferred-passage rank |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| State 0 | P3-H1N1 | B05 / 18 | 1 |\n| State 1 | P9-H1N1 | E04 / 131 | 2 |\n| State 2 | P3-H1N1 | B02 / 21 | 2 |\n\nAll three selected examples happen to be from H1N1-labeled wells. Selection\nallowed both Control and H1N1; no preference for H1N1 was applied. Every state\nalso occurs in Control cells. The image examples are not a treatment comparison.\n\n### Original pixels and display\n\nEach record identifies the original ND2 path and SHA-256, frame 0, original\nobject ID, nuclear coordinates, crop bounds and calibration. Existing nuclear\nmaximum-intensity coordinates match the original DAPI pixel exactly. The saved\nfour-channel NPZ crops preserve native uint16 pixels, without denoising,\nbackground subtraction, local contrast, cell erasure or generated content.\n\nViews show a common 90 x 90 micrometre field centered on the midpoint of the\nrecorded whole-cell bounding box, adjusted only to stay within the original\nimage. Native integer crops slightly exceed 90 micrometres; plot axes display\nexactly 90 micrometres. All selected recorded whole-cell bounding boxes fit\ninside the native crops. This recorded bounding box is not a verified mask.\nNeighboring cells remain visible; arrows locate the one target object in each\nview. Each scale bar is 20 micrometres. Calibration is read from each ND2\n(P3 approximately 0.324081 micrometres/pixel; P9 0.325).\n\nOne fixed linear range per acquired channel is applied to all candidates and\nall states. Bounds are the pooled 0.5th and 99.8th percentiles of the native\npixels in the twelve shortlisted crops, fixed before visual acceptance or\nrejection. There is no per-cell or per-group range and gamma is 1. Values\noutside these display bounds clip visually; underlying uint16 arrays are\nunchanged. Display-clipping fractions are reported separately from acquisition\nsaturation flags. Image selection/display is descriptive; three chosen cells\ncannot establish population intensity differences, and acquisition/batch\ndifferences remain possible.\n\nThe main figure shows the same target as a merged view and DAPI view. The merge\nuses TRITC red, FITC green and DAPI blue. Figure S7J-L additionally shows each\nacquired channel separately, including CY5 as technical context only. Channel\nnames are physical acquisition labels: the existing CY5/TRITC compartment\nannotation discrepancy is not resolved by appearance or renamed silently.\n\n### Limits and consistency\n\nState 0 retains its original extreme-feature flag (all 28 primary State 0\nrecords have this flag). The selected image contains one visually identifiable\ntarget nucleus, but original segmentation masks are unavailable. A real image\nand correct coordinate mapping do not verify the measured object boundary or\nprove that unusual measurements are biological. The examples are therefore\ndescribed as illustrative target objects assigned to the existing states.\n\nThe 98-feature primary PCA/response results remain separate from the existing\n97-feature state representation. State proportions, effects, P values, FDR\nvalues, group assignments and raw measurements are unchanged. No new biological\nresponse criterion, biological conclusion, or experiment is introduced.\n\n### Reproduction and source records\n\nRun `script/run_image_revision.py --dpi 600` to rebuild Figure 4, Table S8,\nFigure S7, legends, combined main PDF and validations. `script/run_all.py`\nalso includes the updated image workflow. Unchanged scripts and results are\ncarried forward in this isolated revision. `script/original_code_archive.zip`\ncontains historical source code; it is retained for provenance, not used as\nthe current rendering entry point.\n\n`selected_representative_images.csv`, `candidate_ranking.csv`,\n`visual_review_log.csv`, `representative_feature_values.csv`,\n`display_settings.json` and the native pixel crops identify every source and\nselection decision. These are also packaged in the Table S8 workbook/companion\nZIP. Original source descriptions under `result/_sources` remain historical\nrecords of the previous placeholder figure; current documentation is here.\n"
